Lyra Docs internal DOCX engine

This package includes a modified derivative of the Apache-2.0 portions of
@docx-editor.dev/core 2.31.0, copyright 2026 EigenPal Inc., from:
https://github.com/eigenpal/docx-editor
Commit: d22e3b4f02d4d0b73d7964114d077b286f207742

Lyra modifications provide explicit module preparation for document features,
DOM presentation, editing commands and native input; split shared pure helpers;
preserve a single implementation of each store operation; and project the
locale catalog to the exact TOC title values used by the engine. Each modified
source file is identified in scripts/engine-source.lock.json and carries a
modification notice in the distributed patch.

The Apache-2.0 license, original upstream notices and HarfBuzz license are in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md also identifies bundled dependencies.
Lyra's original component and adapter code remains under its MIT license.

Reproduction inputs are shipped in scripts/engine-source.lock.json and
scripts/engine/. The lock identifies the immutable upstream archive, selected
source files, exact patch, prepared sources, build dependencies and assets.
Maintainers run the package build with the recorded Node, pnpm and Vite versions.
It verifies and prepares the source in a temporary directory, builds the engine,
and removes that directory. LYRA_DOCX_SOURCE_ARCHIVE may name a previously
acquired archive; it undergoes the same complete integrity checks.

The published package already contains dist/engine and the static editor CSS.
Consumer installation performs no source acquisition or compilation. Engine
implementation entry points are internal and are not upstream API substitutes.
